      ":question/problem": "![](images/91/919a3000b77a74684c6e8f04a610c484c784e136575eff06cab2a764a6b7976f.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[0, 9]$. The graph of $f^{\u2032}(x)$, the derivative of $f(x)$, is shown above, where the area of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $6$, $7$, and $2$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[0, 9]$ given that $f(0) = 0$."
